@startuml
title MODRISS Release Cycle — From Accepted Increments to the Next Release

skinparam backgroundColor #F5F3ED
skinparam shadowing false

start
repeat
  :Define release outcome hypothesis, scope,\ncompatibility policy and target cadence;

  repeat
    repeat
      :Select and deliver one bounded vertical increment;
      :Accept exact CIM, PIM, PSM, generated artifacts\nand verification evidence at G2–G5;
    repeat while (Another increment needed for candidate?) is (yes)
    -> no;

    :Assemble immutable release candidate;
    :Check compatibility, security, quality, cost,\ncapacity, recovery and operational readiness;
  repeat while (G6 release authorization rejected?) is (yes — correct at authoritative source)
  -> no — authorized;

  :Promote progressively through approved environments;
  if (A stop threshold is breached?) then (yes)
    :Stop or roll back;
    :Keep the last accepted operating baseline;
    :Create a corrective increment or release;
  else (no)
    :Complete handover and post-deployment checks;
    :Accept the new operating baseline at G7;
  endif

  repeat
    :Operate the accepted baseline and capture one\noperational work item in WP-30;
    :Classify purpose, emergency status and class of service;
    :Replenish and pull under WP-31 WIP, capacity and SLE policies;
    :Verify the result and choose exactly one disposition:\noperations-only, bounded MDE/release, or planned release;
  repeat while (No release selected and retirement not authorized?) is (continue pull flow)
  -> release or retirement selected;
  :Form the next release hypothesis only from explicitly\nselected roadmap or operational work;
  note right
    The currently accepted release continues to run.
    Operations-only work remains in Phase 3. The next pass
    creates a later release; it does not restart the lifecycle.
  end note
repeat while (Retirement authorized?) is (no — begin next selected release)
-> yes;

:Enter Phase 4 retirement workflow;
stop
@enduml
